\par
ATTRIB [\i named shortcut .lnk file\i0 ] +a -h +s +r \f1  \f0 [Note: All pre-existing files should\f1  \f0 already have the attributes set this way.  Use the ATTRIB command without arguments\f1  \f0 to see the current status of all .lnk files.]\page Note: The reason for the attribute change is to prevent Windows from attempting to\f1  \f0 "guess" for new values of any of these parameters should something be set wrong,\f1  \f0 such as failing to set the PDP-8_DRIVE environment variable as directed.  Without\f1  \f0 the environment variable in effect, some of these parameters cannot be set.  By\f1  locking down\f0  the parameters, copies of the \f1 P?S \f0 Advanced SIMH PDP-8 simulator package\f1  will not be accidentally\f0  modified.  Should there be a reason to change any parameter, the\f1  \f0 read-only attribute of the shortcut can temporarily be changed from within the\f1  \f0 properties of the shortcut itself to allow updating.  After all changes are\f1  \f0 performed, ensure the attributes are set as documented here.\par
\par
Note: Windows does not provide a graphical interface to control the System attribute\f1  \f0 bit; only a command prompt can accomplish this.  Note that .lnk files with the\f1  S\f0 ystem attribute bit will not show in a DIR command at an MS-DOS prompt; however,\f1  \f0 these files will be revealed by the ATTRIB command as well as in Windows as icon\f1 /link properties\f0 .\par
